('oVcPZgl','Nc3','1. Nc3 e2 (bxa2 $144 2. Nxa2 e2 3. Nc1 $18) 2. Bg3+ $3 (2. Ba7+ $143 Kf1 3. Nxe2 bxa2 4. Ng3+ Kg2 5. Bd4 Kxg3 $11) Kxg3 3. Nxe2+ Kf2 (Kf3 $144 4. Nd4+ Ke4 5. Nxb3 $18) 4. Nc1 (4. Nc3 $143 Ke3 5. axb3 Kd4 6. Ne2+ Ke3 7. Ng3 Kd3 $11) b2 (bxa2 $144 5. Nxa2 Ke3 6. Ke6 Kd4 7. Kd6 Kc4 8. Kc6 Kb3 9. Kb6 Kxa2 10. Kxa6 $18) 5. Nd3+ Ke3 6. Nxb2 Kd4 7. Ke6 Kc3 8. Nd3 $3 Kxd3 9. Kd5 Kc2 10. Kc6 Kc3 11. Kc5 Kb2 12. Kb6 Ka3 13. Ka5 $18 {Two paradoxical piece sacrifices aimed at gaining a single tempo each. 8.Sd3!! luring Black into a famous Grigoriev pawn ending is the highlight of this study.}'),
('qCruu5B','Rf3','1. Rf3+ (1. Rf1 $143 f6 $1 2. Rxf6 (2. Ke7 $144 Nb6 (c2 $144 3. Kxf6 e4 4. g5 e3 5. gxh6 e2 6. Ra1 Kd2 $11) 3. Kxf6 Nd5+ 4. Kxe5 Ne3 $11) c2 3. Rd6+ Ke4 4. Rc6 Kf4 5. Rxc2 Kxg4 6. Re2 Kxh5 7. Rxe5+ Kg4 $11) Ke4 $1 (Kd2 $144 2. g5 hxg5 3. h6 c2 4. Rf2+ Kd3 5. Rxc2 Kxc2 6. h7 $18) 2. Rxc3 (2. Rf1 $143 f6 3. Rxf6 c2 4. Rc6 Kf4 5. Rxc2 Kxg4 6. Re2 Kxh5 $11) Kf4 3. Rc4+ $1 e4 (Kg5 $144 4. Rb4 e4 5. Rxe4 Nb6 6. Rb4 Nd5 7. Rb5 $18) 4. Rxe4+ $1 (4. Ke7 $143 Kxg4 5. Rxe4+ Kxh5 6. Kxf7 Kg5 $1 $11) Kxe4 5. g5 Kf5 6. gxh6 Kf6 7. Kd7 $1 (7. Ke8 $143 Nb6 $1 {Zugzwang} (Nc7+ $143 8. Kf8 Ne6+ 9. Kg8 $18) 8. Kf8 Nd7+ 9. Kg8 Kg5 $11) Nb6+ 8. Ke8 $1 {Zugzwang} Nd5 9. Kf8 Ne7 10. h7 $18'),
