('7K1Flm4','Ke4','1. Ke4 $1 (1. Rxc3 $143 Rxa5 2. Rb3 Rf5+ $1 3. Ke4 Rf7 $1 $19) ({Thematic try:} 1. Ke3 $143 c2 $1 2. Rxc2 Rxa5 3. Rb2 Re5+ $1 4. Kd4 Rd5+ $1 5. Ke4 Rd7 $1 6. Ke5 Kg8 $1 7. Ke6 Rh7 $1 8. Kd6 Kf8 $1 9. Kc5 Rh5+ {(Rf7)} 10. Kb6 Rf5 $1 $19) c2 $1 (Kg6 $144 2. Kd3 $11) 2. Rxc2 Ra4+ $1 {now, very important switchback of wK -} 3. Kf3 $3 {This switch-back is the only way as demonstrated in the thematic tries and by the following main line,} Rxa5 4. Rb2 $1 Rf5+ 5. Ke4 Rf7 {In contrast of the thematic try wK has access to the group of black pawns} 6. Ke5 Kg8 ({main} Kg6 $144 {would eventually lead to the same play} 7. Ke6 $1 Rf6+ 8. Ke7 $1 (8. Kd7 $143 c5 $1 9. Kc7 b6 $19) Rf7+ 9. Ke6 Kg7 10. Kd6 $1 Kf8 11. Rh2 $1 Ke8 12. Rh8+ Rf8 13. Rh7 $1 Rf6+ 14. Kc5 Rf5+ 15. Kd6 Rf7 16. Rh8+ Rf8 17. Rh7 $11) 7. Kd6 $1 {This move was possible in the thematic try (see 8. Kd6) only with the black rook on h7 which would prevent white''s next only move} (7. Ke6 $143 Kf8 $19 {and white is too late by a single tempo to get the main line''s positional draw}) Kf8 8. Rh2 $1 Ke8 9. Rh8+ Rf8 10. Rh7 $1 Rf6+ 11. Kc5 Rf5+ 12. Kd6 Rf7 13. Rh8+ Rf8 14. Rh7 Rf6+ 15. Kc5 Rf7 16. Rh8+ Kd7 17. Kb6 $1 $11 {. To characterize a quality of this study is sufficient to note a wonderful, unexpected move 3.Kf3!!}'),
