('0oqesTS','Bf3','1. Bf3 (1. Kh4 $143 d1=Q 2. b8=Q Qh5+ $1 3. Kxh5 Qxg6+ 4. Kh4 Qg5+ 5. Kh3 Qh5#) Qf1 (Qh1+ $144 2. Bxh1 d1=Q+ 3. Kh4 $1 Qxh1+ 4. Kg4 e6 5. Qd7+ Kxg6 6. Qe8+ $11) 2. Qg4 d1=Q 3. Bxd1 Qh1+ 4. Qh4 Qxd1+ 5. g4 (5. Qg4 $143 Qh1+ 6. Qh4 Qxb7 $19) Qb1 6. e4 (6. Qh2 $143 Qxb7 7. Kh4 e6 $19) (6. c6 $143 Qxg6#) Qxb7 (Qxe4 $144 7. g5 Qxg6+ 8. Kg4 Qe4+ (fxg5 $144 9. Qh1 $1 Qe6+ 10. Kg3 $11) (hxg5 $144 9. Qe1 $1 f5+ 10. Kg3 f4+ $11) 9. Kg3 Qd3+ 10. Kh2 Qc2+ 11. Kg3 Qb3+ 12. Kh2 hxg5 13. Qe4 $11) 7. Qg5 $3 hxg5 8. c6 Qb5 9. axb5 a4 10. b6 a3 11. b7 (11. bxc7 $143 a2 12. c8=Q a1=Q $19 {mates.}) a2 12. b8=Q a1=Q 13. Qb1 Qa8 (Qa3 $144 14. Qb3 $1 $11) 14. Qb8 Qa2 15. Qb2 Qg8 16. Qb8 Qh8+ {The black queen appears in all four corners during the solution!} 17. Qxh8+ Kxh8 18. g7+ (18. Kh6 $143 f5 $1 $19) Kh7 (Kxg7 $144 $11 {stalemate.}) 19. g8=Q+ Kxg8 20. Kg6 Kf8 21. Kf5 Kf7 $11 {stalemate.}'),
('W9UCk3I','d8=Q','1. d8=Q+ $1 ({Thematic try} 1. f8=Q $143 Kxh3 2. Qh8 (2. Qa3+ $144 Nf3 3. Bxe5 Qg4 $19 {with mate.}) Qxh8 3. Bxh8 Nxe6 4. Bxe5 c5 $1 (a4 $143 5. Bxc7 a3 6. Kg1 $1 a2 7. Be5 $11) 5. Bc7 a4 6. Bxb6 a3 7. Bxc5 (7. Ba5 $144 Kg3 8. Bc3 Kf3 $19) a2 8. Bg1 $1 Kg4 $1 (a1=Q $143 9. d8=Q Nxd8 $11 {stalemate.}) 9. Bd4 Nxd4 10. d8=Q a1=Q+ 11. Kg2 Qb2+ $19) Kxh3 2. Qh8 Qxh8 3. Bxh8 Nxe6 4. Bxe5 c5 $1 5. Bc7 a4 (b5 $144 6. Bxa5 $11) 6. Bxb6 a3 (c4 $144 7. Bc5 $11) 7. Bxc5 a2 8. Bg1 $1 (8. f8=Q $143 Nxf8 $1 9. Bd4 Kg3 {(g4)} 10. Kg1 Kf3 {(f4)} 11. Kf1 Ke4 12. Ba1 Kd3 13. Ke1 Kc2 14. Ke2 Ne6 $19) Kg4 (a1=Q $144 9. f8=Q Nxf8 $11 {stalemate.}) (Kg3 $144 9. Bh2+ Kf3 10. Be5 $11) 9. Bd4 Nxd4 10. f8=Q a1=Q+ 11. Kg2 Qb2+ 12. Qf2 $1 {=. Compare with the end of the thematic try. Nice study with the interesting content. Of course, the technical weakness is 5 captures in the first 4 moves. But can "close eyes", because here have clear realization of the logical idea.}'),
('VxxoPEI','c5','1. c5 $1 (1. bxa5 $143 bxc4 2. Bxf4 c3 3. Be5 cxb2 4. Bxb2 Rxa5 5. f4 Rc5 6. Ke3 Rc2 7. Bf6 b2 8. Bxb2 Rxb2 9. Nf2 Kb5 10. Nd3 Rb3 11. Ke4 Rxa3 12. Ne5 Ra7 13. Kd5 Ra4 14. f5 Rf4 $11) Rh6 $1 (Rc6 $144 2. bxa5 $18) 2. gxh6 (2. Bxf4 $143 Raa6 $1 3. gxh6 Rxh6 $11) Ra6 3. c6 $3 ({Thematic try} 3. Bxf4 $143 Rxh6 $1 4. Bxh6 (4. Ng3 $144 Rh2+ 5. Ke3 Rxb2 6. Ne4 Kxa3 7. c6 Rc2 8. c7 b2 9. Nd2 Kxb4 $11) f5 5. Be3 f4 6. Kg2 fxe3 7. Ng3 e2 8. Nxe2 $11 {stalemate} (8. Ne4 $143 $19 {and impossible Nc5#, because wP on c5})) Rxc6 4. Bxf4 Rxh6 (f5 $144 5. h7 Rc2+ 6. Ke3 Rh2 7. Nf2 Rxh7 8. Nd3 Re7+ 9. Be5 Rxe5+ 10. Kd4 f4 11. Nc5+ $18) 5. Bxh6 f5 6. Be3 $1 f4 7. Kg2 $1 fxe3 8. Ng3 e2 9. Ne4 e1=Q 10. Nc5#'),
