('HAml4E5','h7','1. h7 $1 (1. h5 $143 $2 Nf6 2. Kf7 Kg5 3. h7 Nxh7 4. gxh7 Bf6 5. Kxe6 $11) (1. Kxg8 $143 $2 Kxg6 2. h7 Bf6 $19) Bf6+ (Nh6 2. Kxh6) 2. Kf8 $1 (2. Kf7 $143 $2 Nh6+ $19) (2. Kxg8 $143 $2 Kxg6 $19) Ne7 $1 (Nh6 $144 3. g7 $18) 3. g7 Ng6+ 4. Kf7 $1 (4. Kg8 $143 $2 Kg4 $1 5. Kf7 Bxg7 6. Kxg7 Kh5 $11) Nh8+ (Ne5+ $144 5. Kg8 Ng6 6. h5 $1 $18) 5. Kg8 Kg6 (Ng6 $144 6. h5 $18) (Bxg7 $144 6. Kxg7 Ng6 7. h5 $18) 6. h5+ $1 (6. gxh8=Q $143 $2 Bxh8 7. Kxh8 (7. h5+ Kf6 8. Kxh8 Kf7) Kf7 8. h5 e5 9. h6 $11) Kh6 7. gxh8=B $18 $1 (7. gxh8=Q $143 $2 Be5 $1 8. Qxe5 $11) (7. gxh8=N $143 $2 e5 8. Nf7+ Kxh5 9. Nd6 Kg6 10. Ne8 Bh8 11. Kxh8 Kf7 $11)'),
('EiVGq6K','f7','1. f7 $1 (1. Be5+ $143 $2 Kc8 2. f7 Kd7 $11) Nd6 $1 (N8g7+ $144 2. Kg6 Kc8 (Nf8+ $144 3. Kxg7 Nd7 4. Kg6 Kc8 5. Kf5 Kd8 6. Bb4 $18) 3. Bxg7 Kd7 4. Kf6 Kd6 5. Bh6 Kd7 6. Bc1 Nf8 7. Ba3 Nh7+ 8. Kf5 Kd8 9. Kg6 $18) (N8c7 $144 2. bxc7+ Kxc7 3. Bb4 Kd7 4. Kg6 b6 5. Kf6 b5 6. Ba3 $18) 2. Be5 Ka8 $1 3. Bxd6 Nd8 (Nf4+ $144 4. Kg4 (4. Kh6 Ne6 5. Bb4 Kb8 6. Kg6 Kc8 7. Kf6 Kd7 8. Ba3) Ne6 5. Bc5 Kb8 6. Kf5 $18) 4. f8=N $1 (4. f8=Q $2) (4. f8=B $2 Nc6) Ne6 $1 5. Nd7 $1 (5. Ng6 $143 $2 Nf4+ 6. Nxf4 $11) (5. Nh7 $144 $2 Ng5 6. Nf8 (6. Nf6 $143 Ne4 $1 7. Ne8 Nf6+ $1 8. Nxf6 $11) Ne6 7. Nd7 $18 {Repeat the position. Loss of time.}) Nc5 $1 (Nf8 $144 6. Ne5 Ng6 {(Cd7 transpose)} 7. Nc4 Ne5 $18 {transpose main line} 8. Na3) 6. Ne5 $1 (6. Nf6 $143 $2 Ne4 $11) (6. Nb8 $143 $2 Nd7 $11) (6. Bxc5 $2) (6. Nxc5 $2) Nd7 (Nd3 $144 7. Nc4 Nb2 8. Na3 Nc4 $18 {transpose to main line}) 7. Nc4 $1 Ne5 8. Na3 $1 (8. Na5 $143 $2 Nc4 $11) (8. Nd2 $143 $2 Nc4 $11) (8. Ne3 $143 $2 Nc4 $11) (8. Bxe5 $2) (8. Nxe5 $2) Nc4 9. Nb5 $1 Nxb6 (Na3 $144 10. Bxa3 $18) (Ne3 $144 10. Kg6 Nc2 11. Kf7 Nd4 12. Nc7+ Kb8 13. Ke8 Kc8 14. Bg3 Nf5 15. Be5 Ne3 16. Nb5 $18) (Nxd6 $144 10. Nxd6 Kb8 11. Kg4 (11. Kg6 Ka8 12. Kf6 Kb8 13. Ke7 Ka8 14. Kd7 Kb8 15. Nc4 Ka8 16. Na5 Kb8 17. Kd8 Ka8 18. Nc6 $1 bxc6 19. Kc7) Ka8 12. Nb5 Kb8 13. Na7 Ka8 14. Kf4 Kb8 15. Ke4 Ka8 16. Kd5 Kb8 17. Kd6 Ka8 18. Nc6 bxc6 19. Kc7 c5 20. b7+ Ka7 21. b8=Q+ Ka6 22. Qb6#) 10. Nc7+ Ka7 (Kb8 $144 {<main>} 11. Nd5+ Ka7 12. Bc5 $18) 11. Bc5 $18 {"An original realisation of a S-vs.-S perpetual attack idea. By precise manoeuvres W, who has to win, avoids positionally drawing. The introductory play with its S-promotion has been adroitly constructed."} Kb8 12. Bxb6'),
('h5ieInI','Nf6','1. Nf6+ Kg7 2. Ne8+ (2. Nh5+ $143 Kh6 3. g7 Rf1 4. Rg6+ Kxh5 5. Rg5+ Kh4 6. Rg4+ Kh3 7. Rg3+ Kh4 $11) Kh6 (Kg8 $144 3. g7 e1=Q+ 4. Rxe1 Rg2 5. Rh1 Kf7 6. Rh8 $18) 3. g7 Rf1 (Rg2 $144 4. Rh1+ Rh2 5. Rxh2+ Kg6 6. g8=Q#) 4. Rg6+ Kh5 (Kxg6 $144 5. g8=Q+ Kh6 6. Qg7+ Kh5 7. Nf6+ Rxf6 8. Kxf6 $18) 5. Nf6+ (5. Rg5+ $143 Kh4 6. Rg4+ Kh3 7. Rg3+ (7. Re4 $144 e1=Q 8. Rxe1 Rxe1+ $11) Kh4 $11) Rxf6 6. Kxf6 (6. Rg5+ $143 Kxg5 7. g8=Q+ Rg6 8. Qd8+ Kg4 9. Qd2 Kf3 10. Qd3+ Kf2 11. Qf5+ Ke3 $1 12. Qf4+ Kd3 13. Qd4+ Kc2 14. Qe3 Rg2 15. Ke4 Kd1 $1 16. Qd3+ Kc1 $11) e1=Q 7. Rg5+ $1 (7. g8=Q $143 Qa1+ 8. Kf7 Qa7+ 9. Kf8 Qa8+ 10. Kg7 (10. Kf7 $144 Qa7+ 11. Kf6 Qa6+ 12. Kf5 Qd3+ 13. Kf6 Qa6+ 14. Qe6 Qxe6+ 15. Kxe6 Kxg6 $11) Qxg8+ 11. Kxg8 Kxg6 $11) Kh6 $1 (Kh4 $144 8. g8=Q $18) 8. g8=N+ (8. g8=Q $143 Qe5+ 9. Rxe5 $11) Kh7 9. Kf7 $18 {"This excellent classic study shows Matous1 notorious technique. And fortunate favours the bold!. I have studied over hundred other studies with a RN vs. Q win; only a few of them have a quiet move and the connection with underpromotion is probably entirely original." Study of the year 1997}'),
('51yE5a3','Rb8','1. Rb8+ Kh7 2. Rb7+ Kg8 3. Nf5 $1 Qf2+ 4. Kh1 Qxe2 (Qxf5 $144 5. Bc4+ Kh8 6. Rb8+ Kg7 7. Rb7+ Kg6 8. Rb6+ $11) (Nxe2 $144 5. Nh6+ Kh8 6. Nf7+ Kg7 7. Ne5+ Kg8 8. Rb8+ Kh7 9. Rb7+ $11) 5. Ne7+ Kf7 6. Nd5+ Kf8 7. Rb8+ Kg7 8. Rb7+ Kh6 9. Rb6+ Kg5 10. Rg6+ Kf5 11. Rf6+ Kg4 (Ke5 $144 12. Re6+ Kxe6 $11) 12. Rg6+ Kh4 13. Rh6+ Kg3 14. Rg6+ $11'),
('ASntdXw','Bg7','1. Bg7+ Kb3 2. Bf7+ Ka3 3. Nd3 Qh8 4. Be5 Qf6 5. Bd5 $18 (5. Bc4 $143 Qf5 $11)'),
('gsSzfgg','e6','1. e6 Nd6 2. f6 Ne4 (Ke8 3. Ba3 $11 {positional draw.}) 3. f7 Nc5+ 4. Kc3 Rf2 5. f8=Q+ Rxf8 6. e7+ Kxe7 7. Kc4 Kd6 (Nb7 $144 8. Ba3+ Nd6+ 9. Kd5 $11) (Rf5 $144 8. Ba3 Kd6 $11 {transpose}) (Rc8 $144 8. Ba3 Kd6 $11) 8. Ba3 Rf5 (Rc8 $144 9. Bb4 $11) 9. Kb5 $11 {"A miniature in classic style! The hope that White places in his two passed pawns seems to go up in smoke almost at once, but a double pawn sacrifice followed by the quiet 7.Kc4 forces Black into an irrevocable pin in 4 variations (mirror symmetry on c5 and d6). It''s amazing that the position after 7.Kc4 has not been discovered before! A similar fourfold pin has been shown by .Herbstman (Shakhmaty vSSSR 1953, 4th HM), but the mechanism is comparatively clumsy." "PS: After the confirmation period a serious anticipation was pointed out to the judge. E. Pogosyants, 1983 [0313.20e2e8]"}'),
('UUlpVwT','Rd8','1. Rd8+ (1. Bg2+ $143 Kd4 2. Rd8+ Kc3 3. Rc8+ Bc5+ $19) Ke4 (Kc6 $144 2. Bxe2 Bb6+ 3. Kxc2 Bxd8 4. Bf3+ $11) 2. Re8+ (2. Bg2+ $143 Kf4 3. Rf8+ Kg5 4. Re8 Be3+ $19) Kd3 3. Rxe2 (3. Bxe2+ $143 Kc3 $19) Be3+ 4. Rd2+ Kc3 $11'),
('TFD72sx','e7','1. e7+ (1. Nf6 $143 Rh4 2. Bf5 Rh2+ 3. Ka1 Rf2 4. Nd7+ Ke7 5. Bg4 Rf4 $11) Kf7 (Ke8 $144 2. Nf6+ Kxe7 3. Nd5+ $18) 2. Be6+ Ke8 3. Bf5 $1 (3. Bd5 $143 Rb8 4. Bc6+ Kf7 5. Bd5+ Kg7 $11) Rb6 $1 (Rb8 $144 4. Bg6+ Kd7 5. e8=Q+ Rxe8 6. Nf6+ $18) 4. Bd3 $1 (4. Bc2 $143 Re6 5. Bxa4+ Kf7 6. Bb3 Ke8 7. Bxe6 $11) (4. Bg4 $143 Rb5 5. Bd1 Re5 $11) a3 $1 (Kf7 $144 5. Bc4+ Ke8 6. Be2 Rb8 7. Bh5+ $18) (Kd7 $144 5. Bc2 Ra6 6. Ka3 Ra8 7. Bxa4+ $18) 5. Ka1 $1 (5. Kxa3 $143 Re6 6. Bb5+ Kf7 7. Bc4 Ke8 8. Bxe6 $11) Kd7 $1 (a2 $144 6. Be2 Rb8 7. Bh5+ $18) 6. Bc2 $1 (6. Be2 $143 Rb8 7. Bg4+ Kd6 $11) (6. Bf5+ $143 Ke8 7. Bc2 Kf7 8. Ba4 Rb8 $11) Ra6 7. Bf5+ Ke8 8. Bd3 Rb6 9. Be2 Rb8 10. Bh5+ Kd7 11. e8=Q+ Rxe8 12. Nf6+ $18'),
('2OjAa71','Ne5','1. Ne5+ Ke4 (Kd4 $144 2. g6 Bh6 3. Nf3+ $1 $18 Nxf3 4. Bxf3 $18) 2. g6 (2. Nf7 $143 Bxg5+ 3. Nxg5+ Kf4 $11) Bh6 3. Nf7 Bg7 (Bf8 $144 4. Bd1 Kf5 5. Bc2+ Kf6 6. Nc7 Nxg6 7. Ne8+ Kxf7 8. Bb3#) 4. Bd1 Kf5 5. Bc2+ Kf6 6. Nb6 Nxg6 7. Nd7+ Kxf7 (Ke6 $144 8. Bxg6 $18) 8. Bb3# {"The parallel synthesis of a pair of pure mates brilliantly realised in a light setting. A masterly study."}'),
('KOB3DEb','Rc4','1. Rc4 (1. Rc2 $143 Qd7 2. Rf1 Qf5 3. Rf3 (3. Rf4 $144 Qc5 4. Rd4 Qf8 5. Rf4 Qc5 $11) Qc5 4. Rff2 Qf5 5. Rf3 Qc5 6. Re3 Qf8 7. Rf3 Qc5 $11) (1. Rc3 $143 Qd7 2. Rd5 (2. Re1 $144 Qe6 3. Ree3 Qc6 4. Rf3 Qa8 5. Rc1 Qe8 6. Rcf1 Qxg6 7. Rh3 $11) (2. Rd4 $144 Qe8 3. Re4 (3. Re3 $144 Qa8 $11) Qa8 4. Rc1 Qf8 5. Rf4 Qc5 $11) Qe8 3. Re3 Qf8 4. Rf5 (4. Rf3 $144 Qe8 5. Rf1 Qxg6 $11) Qa8 $11) (1. Rc5 $143 Qd7 2. Rd4 (2. Re1 $144 Qe6 $11) Qe8 3. Re4 Qa8 4. Rc1 Qf8 5. Rf4 Qc5 $11) (1. Rc6 $143 Qd7 2. Re1 Qe6 3. Rf1 Qf5 $11) (1. Ra1 $143 Qa5 $11) Qd7 (Qb8 $144 2. Rf1 (2. Re1 $143 Qa8 $11) Qa8 3. Re4 Qc8 4. Re7 Qa8 5. Rb7 Qe8 6. Rbf7 $18) 2. Rd5 (2. Rf1 $143 Qf5 $11) (2. Re1 $143 Qc6 3. Ree4 Qa8 4. Rc1 Qf8 5. Rf4 Qe8 6. Rcf1 Qxg6 $11) (2. Rd2 $143 Qe8 3. Re4 Qa8 4. Rd1 Qf8 5. Rf4 Qe8 $11) (2. Rdd4 $143 Qe8 3. Re4 Qa8 4. Rc1 Qf8 5. Rf4 Qe8 $11) (2. Rd6 $143 Qe8 3. Re4 Qf8 $11) Qc7 (Qe8 $144 3. Re4 Qa8 (Qxg6 $144 4. Rd8+ Kxh7 5. Rh4+ $18) 4. Re1 Qf8 5. Rf5 Qa8 6. Rf3 Qb8 7. Rff1 Qa8 8. Re4 $18) 3. Rf5 (3. Rd6 $143 Qd7 4. Re4 Qc8 5. Re1 Qf8 $11) (3. Rc6 $143 Qb8 4. Rb6 Qf8 5. Rf5 Qa8 $11) (3. Re5 $143 Qb8 4. Rc1 (4. Re1 $144 Qa8 $11) (4. Rb5 $144 Qa8 $11) Qf8) (3. Rd2 $143 Qb8 4. Rd1 Qa8 5. Re4 Qf8 6. Rf4 Qa8 7. Rf3 Qe8 8. Rdf1 Qxg6 9. Rh3 Qe8 10. Kxh2 $11) Qc5 (Qb8 $144 4. Rf1 (4. Rc1 $143 Qe8 $11) Qa8 5. Re4 $18) 4. Rf2 Qf5 5. Re4 Qc8 6. Re1 (6. Rf1 $143 Qa8 $11) Qa8 7. Rf3 Qb8 8. Rff1 Qa8 9. Re4 Qb8 10. Re7 Qa8 11. Rb7 Qc8 12. Rbf7 $18 {Possibilities are based primarily on stalemate via threats to check on the 1st rank or on g2, but there is also the possibility of a mate threat (on gl) or simply to capture wPg6, lifting the stalemate, but adequately restoring the material balance and destroying W''s own back-rank mate threats. As an example of all this, if bQ is on a8, then one wR must stand on the first rank and the other wR on the b7-f3 diagonal. With bQe8 (for check or Qxg6) W needs to have one wR to block check and the other to meet... Qxg6 + ; with a check on the h-file (after R8 + , Kxh7;). With bQf8 however, the block must be on the f-file itself, as no block on the first rank is possible. The key to W''s win turns out to be the position of mutual zugzwang: bQa8, wRe4 and wRfl. In this position wRe4 cannot move, and if wRfl moves off the f-file, then ..., Qf8; follows, Rf4 is forced, and Qa8; forces the same wR back to e4. Eventually, after the zugzwang in the main line (9. Re4) W wins by safely doubling rooks, a manoeuvre that crops up in the supporting variations as well. "A very refined struggle of wRR against bQ, with hidden stalemate traps. W subtly manoeuvres both wR''s in steps to avoid all Bl''s defensive endeavours ~ and wins by dint of a zugzwang."}'),
('bAMNtvd','g7','1. g7 (1. Rh8 $143 h1=Q $19) (1. Rd1 $143 h1=Q $19) (1. Kb8 $143 Rb5+ 2. Ka7 Kxc7 $19) Ra5 $1 (h1=Q $143 2. g8=Q Kc5 3. Qa2 Rf6 4. Qa3+ Kb6 5. Rd6+ Rxd6 6. Qxd6+ Ka5 7. Qd2+ Ka6 8. Qa2+ Kb5 9. Kb8 $18) 2. Kb8 (2. Rd6+ $143 Kxd6 3. Kd8 Ra8+ $19) Rb5+ 3. Ka7 Ra5+ (Kxc7 $143 4. Rc8+ $1 Kxc8 5. g8=Q+ $18) 4. Kb8 Ra8+ $1 5. Kxa8 h1=Q 6. Rd1 $1 (6. c8=Q+ $143 Kb6+ 7. Kb8 Qh2+ $19) Qg2 7. Rd2 $1 (7. Rg1 $143 Qa2+ 8. Kb8 Qb3+ 9. Kc8 Qg8#) Qf3 8. Rd3 Qe4 9. Rd4 Qe8+ 10. Rd8 Qe4 11. Rd4 Qh1 12. Rd1 $11 {"A miniature whose solution has unquestionable artistic beauty, very well presented."}'),
('h5NIPGs','h6','1. h6 (1. g7 $143 Kxh5 2. Kf7 Ng4 $11) Kg5 $1 2. h7 (2. g7 $143 Kxh6 3. Kf7 Kh7 4. Nd5 (4. Ne4 $144 Ng8 $11) Ng8 $11) Nxh7 3. g7 $1 (3. gxh7 $143 Bf6 4. Ne4+ Kg6 5. Nxf6 Kg7 $11) Nf6 4. Kf7 $1 (4. Ne4+ $143 Kg6 $1 $11) Ng8 $1 (Kf4 $144 5. Nd5+ $18) (Kf5 $144 5. Nd5 Ng4 6. Ne3+ $1 $18) (Kh5 $144 5. Ne4 $1 Ng4 6. Ng3+ Kh4 7. Nf5+ $18) (Kh4 $144 5. Ne4 Ng4 6. Kg6 Ne5+ 7. Kh7 $18) 5. Ne4+ $1 (5. Kxg8 $143 Kg6 $1 6. Ne4 (6. Nd5 $144 Bg5 $1 7. Kh8 Kh6 $1 8. g8=Q (8. Kg8 $144 Kg6 9. Kf8 Bh6 $11) Bf6+ $1 9. Nxf6 $11) Bh4 $1 (Bc7 $143 7. Kf8 $1 $18) (Bb6 $143 7. Kf8 $1 $18) 7. Kh8 Kh6 8. Kg8 Kg6 9. Kf8 Be7+ $1 10. Kg8 Bh4 $11 (Ba3 $144 11. Nf6 Bb2 12. Kf8 Ba3+ $11)) Kf5 6. Kxg8 Kg6 7. Kh8 $1 Kh6 $1 8. Nf2 $1 Bf6 (Bb6 $144 9. Ng4+ $18) 9. Ng4+ $18'),
('X2r8SQl','Nf3','1. Nf3+ Kh1 $1 (Kh3 $144 2. Ng5+ Kg2 3. Bxc5+ $18) 2. Bd4 $3 {with a mate threat} (2. Bxc5 $143 Qa4+ 3. Nd4 Qxd4+ 4. Bxd4 $11 {stalemate}) Qf7+ $1 (Qc7+ $144 3. Ne5 Qc8 (Qb8 $144 4. Rb2 $1 Qf8+ 5. Kg3 Qg7+ 6. Ng4 Qc7+ 7. Be5 Qh7 8. Rd2 $18) 4. Kg3 Qg8+ 5. Ng4 Qb8+ 6. Kh3 Qb3+ 7. Rc3 Qb1 8. Nf2+ Kg1 9. Ne4+ cxd4 10. Rg3+ Kf1 11. Nd2+ $18) (Qb8+ $144 3. Be5 Qf8+ 4. Ke3 Qh6+ 5. Kf2 c4 6. Ra2 Qb6+ 7. Bd4 Qb1 8. Ra1 $18) 3. Ke3 $3 (3. Kg3 $143 Qg6+ 4. Kf4 Qxc2 $19) (3. Ke5 $143 Qe8+ 4. Kf6 Qh8+ 5. Kg5 cxd4 $11) cxd4+ 4. Kf2 $1 Qf4 5. Rc6 $3 {Mutual zugzwang. Black has no good move with his queen.} (5. Re2 $143 Qe3+ $11) (5. Ra2 $143 Qc1 6. Kg3 $5 (6. Ra8 $143 Qc2+ 7. Kg3 Qg6+ 8. Kf4 $19) Qc7+ 7. Kf2 Qc1 8. Re2 d3 9. Re1+ Qxe1+ $11) (5. Rc8 $143 Qe3+ 6. Kg3 Qh6 7. Kf2 Qe3+ 8. Kg3 Qh6 9. Rg8 d3 $11) Qe3+ (d3 $144 {the second thematic echo-like line} 6. Rc8 $3 Qh6 7. Rb8 $1 $18 (7. Ra8 $143 Qg7 $19)) 6. Kg3 {Mutual zugzwang again. Black has to move with a pawn blocking important line.} d3 7. Ra6 $1 Qc1 8. Ra7 $1 $18 (8. Ra8 $143 Qc7+ 9. Kf2 Qb6+ $19)'),
('PD9mTTn','Rg4','1. Rg4+ (1. b7 $143 Rb1 2. Rg4+ Ka3 $11) Ka5 (Ka3 $144 2. Nb5+ $18) 2. b7 Rb1 3. Rg5+ Ka4 4. Nb5 (4. Rb5 $143 d1=Q 5. b8=Q $11) Rxb5 (d1=Q $144 5. Nc3+ Ka3 6. Nxb1+ Qxb1 7. Ra5+ $18) 5. Rxb5 d1=Q (Kxb5 $144 6. b8=Q+ Kc4 7. Qc8+ Kd4 8. Qc2 Ke3 9. Qd1 h2 10. Qh1 $18) 6. b8=Q Qg1+ (h2 $144 7. Qe8 h1=Q 8. Rb7+ Ka3 9. Qa8+ Qa4 10. Qf8+ Ka2 11. Qf2+ $18) (Qg4+ $144 7. Kf8 Qf3+ (Qh4 $144 8. Rb6 $18) 8. Ke7 h2 (Qa3+ $144 9. Ke8 h2 10. Qb6 $18) (Qe4+ $144 9. Re5 $18) 9. Qe8 h1=Q 10. Rb7+ Qc6 11. Qa8+ $18) 7. Kh7 h2 8. Rb4+ Ka3 9. Rb3+ Ka2 10. Rb2+ Ka1 11. Qh8 h1=Q+ 12. Rh2+ Kb1 13. Qb2#')
