('eMD1SUk','b7','1. b7 Qb8 (Kxe7+ $144 2. Kb1 Qb8 3. Rd7+ Kxe6 4. Rxg7 Qa7 5. Rh6+ Kd5 6. Rd7+ Kc5 7. f4+) (Qe8 $144 2. Bh2 e3 3. fxe3 Qxh5 (Kxe7+ $144 4. Re5 Bxe5+ 5. Bxe5 c3 6. b8=Q Qxb8 7. Rd7+ Kxe6 8. Bxb8 Kxd7 $18) 4. b8=Q Kxe6+ 5. Rd4 $18) 2. Kb1 (2. e8=N+ $143 Qxe8 3. Kb1 $11 (3. Bh2 $143 e3 $17)) c3 3. Rd7 (3. Rd8 $143 c2+ 4. Kc1 b2+ 5. Kxb2 Kxe7+ $19) (3. Rdd5 $143 Qa7 4. e8=N+ Ke7 5. Rd7+ Kxe6 6. Nxg7+ Kxd7 7. Rd5+ Ke7 8. Nf5+ Kf7 $19) Qa7 (c2+ $144 4. Kc1 Qa7 5. Rf5+ Kxf5 6. g4+ $18) 4. Rf5+ Kxf5 5. g4+ Kf6 6. g5+ Kf5 7. Rd5+ Be5 8. Rxe5+ Kf4 9. Rxe4+ Kf5 10. Re5+ Kf4 11. Rf5+ Kxf5 12. e4+ Kxe4 (Kf4 $144 13. b8=Q+ Qxb8 14. Bh2+ $18) 13. f3+ Kd3 14. Bxa7 Kd2 15. Be3+ $18 {"Romantic grand design stuff: four-fold ''albino'' moves by a wP. The composer had already done a three-fold version (at the helyabinsk festival). Here White'' play is strengthened with the addition of the fourth thematic line. The moves I.b7! and 2.KM! impress."}'),
