('oFDoy9v','Bb5','1. Bb5+ (1. Bc8+ $143 Ka5 2. Nd2 f1=Q 3. Nxf1 g2 4. Nd2 Na6+ 5. Kc6 Nb8+ 6. Kc5 Na6+ 7. Kd5 Nb4+ (g1=Q $143 8. Nc4+ Kb5 9. Bd7#) 8. Kc5 Na6+ $11) Ka5 2. Nd2 (2. hxg3 $143 Nd7+ 3. Kc6 Nb8+ 4. Kc5 Nd7+ $11) Na6+ 3. Bxa6 g2 4. Bf1 g1=Q 5. h6 (5. e4 $143 Qg7 6. Nc4+ Ka6 7. Nd6+ Ka5 8. Nc4+ (8. Kc6 $143 Qh6 9. Bc4 f1=Q 10. Bxf1 Qc1+ 11. Bc4 Qxa3 $19) Ka6 $11) (5. Kc6 $143 h6 6. e4 Qh1 7. h4 Qg1 8. Nc4+ Ka6 9. Bh3 Qg8 10. Nd6 Qa8+ 11. Kc7 Ka5 12. Nb7+ Qxb7+ 13. Kxb7 $11) Qh1 (e4 $144 6. h4 Qh1 7. Kc6 Qg1 (Qxh4 $144 8. Nc4+ Ka6 9. Nd6+ Ka5 10. Nb7#) 8. h5 Qh1 9. Bb5 $18) 6. e4 (6. h3 $143 e4 7. Kc6 Qg1 $11) Qg1 7. h3 (7. h4 $143 Qh1 8. h5 Qg1 9. Kc6 Qh1 10. Bb5 f1=Q 11. Bxf1 Qg1 12. Nc4+ Ka6 13. Bh3 Qg4 14. Bxg4 $11) Qh1 8. h4 Qg1 9. h5 Qh1 10. Kc6 Qg1 11. Nc4+ Ka6 12. Bh3 Qg8 13. Nd6 Qe6 (Qa8+ $144 14. Kc7 Ka5 15. Nb7+ Qxb7+ (Kb5 $144 16. Bf1#) 16. Kxb7 $18) 14. Bxe6 f1=Q 15. Kc7 Qc1+ 16. Bc4+ Ka5 17. Nb7#'),
('vw0XWqC','Rh8','1. Rh8 (1. Rg8 $143 Kxa7 2. Rg7+ Kb8 3. a6 Re7 4. Rg8+ Kc7 5. Nb6 Qf5 6. Nxd5+ Kd7 7. a7 $11) Kxa7 2. Rh7+ Kb8 3. a6 Re7 (dxc4 $144 4. a7+ Ka8 5. Ka6 Qf6 6. Rh8+ Qxh8 7. Bxe4+ d5 8. Bxd5#) (Qf2 $144 4. Rb7+ Kc8 5. Nb6+ Kd8 6. Rb8+ Ke7 7. Nxd5+ Kf7 8. Bxe4 Qe2+ 9. Kb6 Qxe4 10. a7 Qxd5 11. a8=Q $18) 4. Rh8+ Kc7 5. Nb6 Qf5 (Qb4+ $144 6. Kxb4 Kxb6 7. Bf1 $18) 6. Nxd5+ Kd7 7. Bh3 g4 8. Bxg4 Re6 9. Rd8+ (9. Bxf5 $143 $11) (9. Rh7+ $143 Qxh7 10. Nf6+ Kc7 11. Nxh7 Re5+ 12. Kc4 Re4+ $19 {"A grand over-all concept with fluent play. Black''s two main line of defence explain White''s first move in a totally harmonious way. All that makes endgame composition attractive is combined in this one magnificent study" (RO). "This is really a study after my own heart. A combination of domination, pins, mate and stalemate resources and a crucial first ove, where White has to chooise between seemingly equal rook moves" (JT) .})'),
('3wWvXTE','d8=N','1. d8=N+ Kf6 2. Ra6+ Kg5 3. Nf7+ (3. Ne6+ $2 Kh4 4. Ra4+ Ng4) Kh4 (Nxf7 4. Re6) 4. Ra4+ d4 5. Rxd4+ Ng4 6. Rxg4+ fxg4 7. b8=B $3 (7. b8=Q $2 h1=Q+ 8. Kxh1 e1=Q+ 9. Kg2 Qe4+ 10. Kh2 Qf4+ 11. Qxf4) h1=Q+ 8. Kxh1 e1=Q+ (Kh3 9. Ng5+ Kh4 10. Bg3+ Kxg5 11. f4+ (11. f3 $2 h4 12. Bf2 Kf4 13. fxg4 Kxg4 14. a4 Kf3 15. Bxh4 Ke4) gxf3 12. a4 Kf5 13. a5 Ke4 14. a6 Ke3 15. Kg1 Kd2 16. a7 e1=Q+ 17. Bxe1+ Kxe1 18. a8=Q f2+ 19. Kh2 f1=Q 20. Qh1) 9. Kg2 Qe4+ (g3 10. Bxg3+ Kg4 11. f3+) 10. Kh2 g3+ 11. Bxg3+ Kg4 12. f3+ Kxf3 13. Ng5+ Ke3 14. Bf2+ (14. Nxe4 $2 Kxe4 15. a4 Kd5) Kd3 15. Nxe4 Kxe4 16. a4 Kd5 17. a5 Kc6 18. a6 Kc7 19. Ba7 Kc6 20. a4'),
