('MyY8IAA','Bb3','1. Bb3 (1. d7 $2 Kg6+ 2. Kg8 Rd1 3. Be6 f5 4. Kf8 Kf6 5. Ke8 Kxe6 6. d8=Q Rxd8+ 7. Kxd8 Kd6) Rh2 (Ra1 $5) 2. d7 Kg6+ 3. Kg8 Rd2 4. Bc2+ (4. Ba4 $2 Kf5) (4. Be6 f5) f5 5. Ba4 Kf6 6. Kf8 Rd3 (Ke6 7. Ke8) 7. Bb5 (7. Bc6 $2 Rd6 8. Ke8 Re6+) (7. Ke8 $2 Re3+ 8. Kd8 Rd3) Rd1 $1 (Rd6 8. Bc6) 8. Ke8 (8. Bc6 $2 Rd6 9. Ke8 Re6+ 10. Kd8 Rd6) Re1+ 9. Kd8 Rc1 $1 (Ke6 10. Kc7) (Rd1 10. Bc4 Rc1 11. Bd5) 10. Bc4 (10. Bd3 $2 Kf7) (10. Ba6 $2 Rc6 11. Bb7 Rd6 12. Ke8 Re6+) Rd1 (Rxc4 11. Ke8 Rd4 12. d8=Q+ Rxd8+ 13. Kxd8) 11. Ke8 (11. Kc7 $2 Ke7) Re1+ 12. Kf8 Rd1 13. Bb5 Rd6 14. Bc6 Rd2 15. Ke8 Re2+ 16. Be4'),
('I259UZ2','g8=Q','1. g8=Q Kf1 2. Bh2 (2. Nd2+ $2 Rxd2 3. Bc4+ Ree2 4. Bh2 f2) g1=Q+ 3. Bxg1 Rg2+ 4. Kxf3 Rxg8 5. Be3 $1 (5. Bf2 $2 Rd8 $1 6. Nd2+ Rxd2 7. Bc4+ Ree2 $1 (Rde2 $2 8. Bb5)) Rg2 6. Nd2+ $1 Rxd2 7. Bc4+ Rde2 (Ree2 8. Bxd2 $1) 8. Bf2 $1 Rc1 9. Bxe2#'),
('SPfgdpL','c6','1. c6+ Kb8 2. Bc5+ $1 (2. Bf2+ $2 Bb6 3. Bg3+ Ka7 4. Qa4+ Ba5 5. Bf2+ Kb8 6. Qf4+ Bc7 7. Qb4+ Bb6 8. Bg3+ Ka7 9. Qa3+ Ba5 10. Bf2+ Kb8 11. Qg3+ Bc7 12. Qb3+ Bb6 13. Bg3+ Ka7 14. Qxa2+ Ba5 15. Bf2+ Kb8) (2. Bg1+ $2 Bb6 3. Bh2+ Ka7 4. Qa4+ Ba5 5. Bg1+ Kb8 6. Qf4+ Bc7 7. Qb4+ Bb6 8. Bh2+ Ka7 9. Qa3+ Ba5 10. Bg1+ Kb8 11. Qg3+ Bc7 12. Qb3+ Bb6 13. Bh2+ Ka7 14. Qxa2+ Ba5 15. Bg1+ Kb8 16. Qh2+ Bc7 17. Qb2+ Bb6 18. Bh2+ Ka7 19. Qa3+ Ba5 20. Bg1+ Kb8 21. Qg3+ Bc7 22. Qb3+ Bb6 23. Bh2+ Ka7 24. Qa4+ Ba5) Bb6 3. Bd6+ Ka7 4. Qa4+ Ba5 5. Bc5+ Kb8 (Ka6 6. Qc4#) 6. Qf4+ $1 Bc7 7. Qb4+ Bb6 8. Bd6+ Ka7 9. Qa3+ Ba5 10. Bc5+ Kb8 11. Qg3+ Bc7 12. Qb3+ Bb6 13. Bd6+ Ka7 14. Qxa2+ Ba5 15. Bc5+ Kb8 16. Qh2+ $1 Bc7 17. Qb2+ Bb6 18. Bd6+ Ka7 19. Qa3+ Ba5 20. Bc5+ Kb8 21. Qg3+ $1 Bc7 22. Qb3+ Bb6 23. Bd6+ Ka7 24. Qa4+ Ba5 25. Kh2 $3 (25. Bc5+ $2 Kb8 26. Qb5+ Bb6 27. Bxb6 Qxd7 $1) Bxc6 26. Qxc6 Qf6 (Qg8 27. Bc5+ Kb8 28. Qb5+ Kc7 29. Qxa5+ Kxd7 30. Qa7+ Kc6 31. Qb6+ Kd7 32. Qb7+) 27. Bc5+ Kb8 28. Qc8#'),
('piGTD64','Bd4','1. Bd4 $1 Qb6 $1 (Qc6+ 2. Kb4+ Kb1 3. Qb3+ Kc1 4. Bxe3#) (Qd6 2. Qc4 $1) 2. Bxb6 h1=Q 3. Bd4 Qd1 $1 (Qc1+ 4. Kb4+ Qb2+ $1 5. Bxb2+ Kxb2 6. Qb3+ Kc1 7. Qxe3+ Kd1 8. Qd4+ Ke2 9. Qb2+ Kf1 10. Kc3 $1 f2 11. Kd2 Kg2 12. Qg7+ Kf1 13. Qf6) 4. Qg1 $1 (4. Kc4+ $2 Qxd4+ $1 5. Kxd4 e2 $1) e2 5. Bh8 $1 (5. Qe1 $2 Kb1) (5. Kc4+ $2 Kb1) f2 (Kb1 6. Qb6+ Kc1 7. Qb2#) (e1=Q+ 6. Qxe1 $1 Qxe1+ 7. Kc2+) 6. Qg7 $1 Qc1+ (Kb1 {main}) 7. Kb3+ Kb1 8. Qa1#'),
('Jpep6yp','Kg5','1. Kg5 (1. Ke5 $143 b5 2. d4 b4 3. d5 b3 4. d6 b2 5. d7 b1=Q 6. d8=Q Qe4+ $19) (1. Kxf5 $143 b5 2. d4 b4 3. d5 b3 4. d6 b2 5. d7 b1=Q+ 6. Ke6 Qb8 7. Ke7 Qe5+ 8. Kf8 Qf6+ 9. Ke8 Qe6+ $19) b5 (Kb3 $144 2. Kxf5 Kc3 3. Ke5 Kxd3 4. Kd5 $11) 2. d4 b4 3. d5 Kb5 4. d6 (4. Kf6 $143 Kc5 5. Ke6 b3 6. d6 b2 7. d7 b1=Q 8. d8=Q Qe4+ 9. Kf7 Qd5+ $19) Kc6 5. Kxf5 Kxd6 (b3 $144 6. Ke6 $11) 6. Ke4 $11'),
('nOcmmKY','e7','{A real masterpiece. Starting from a game-like position, both sides must play accurately but White has the last laugh as he forces either perpetual check or a pin-stalemate. There is an attractive thematic try in which White makes the mistake of winning the h4-pawn, which destroys the final stalemate. Although there are a lot of four-rook studies around at the moment, no serious anticipation could be identified. Solving appeal is high as the analysis is fairly straightforward and so the theme of the study is not obscured by dense thickets of variations. Un réel chef d''oeuvre. Commençant par une position de partie, les deux camps doivent jouer de façon précise. Les Blancs ont le dernier mot comme ils forcent l''échec perpétuel ou le pat.par clouage Bien qu''il y ait beaucoup d''études avec quatre tours en ce moment, aucune réelle anticipation ne peut être trouvée. On a vraiment envie de résoudre cette étude comme son analyse est directe et que le thème de l''étude n''est pas obscurici par des variations touffues.} 1. e7 (1. Rh8+ $143 Rf8 $19) Rf1+ $1 (Re5 $144 {1...Re4 is similar} 2. Rh8+ Kd7 3. e8=Q+ Rxe8 4. Rhxe8 b1=Q 5. Rxb1 Kxe8 6. Rb2 $11 {followed by Kg2 is a draw. Black cannot improve his position and exchanging rooks leads to a drawn pawn ending.}) 2. Rxf1 Ra1 3. Rhf6 $1 (3. Rh8+ $143 {is the thematic try:} Kxe7 4. Rh7+ $1 (4. Rhf8 $144 b1=Q {wins for Black here because the f8-rook is under attack and so White cannot take on b1, while continuing to check fails because the black queen controls f5:} 5. R8f7+ Ke6 $1 6. R7f6+ Ke5 $1 7. R6f5+ Qxf5 $19 {and Black wins}) Ke6 $1 {Black''s king must stay on the e-file so as to have the white rook under attack if White doubles rooks on the f-file.} 5. Rh6+ $1 Ke5 $1 6. Rh5+ $1 Ke4 $1 7. Rxh4+ $1 (7. Rhf5 $144 b1=Q 8. R5f4+ Ke5 9. Rxb1 Rxb1+ 10. Kg2 Rb2+ $1 $19 {wins}) Ke3 $1 8. Rhf4 $1 Rc1 $1 $19 {reaches essentially the same position as in the main line after 8...Kd3. However, White then loses because the stalemate defence of the main line is not available.} ({but not} b1=Q $143 9. R4f3+ $1 $11 Ke2 10. Rxb1 $1 Rxb1+ 11. Kg2 $11 {drawing})) Rc1 $1 {The most dangerous move.} (b1=Q $144 4. Rxb1 Rxb1+ 5. Kg2 {draws because the rook is not attacked on f6 and the continuation} Rb2+ 6. Kg1 Rh2 7. Re6 Rxh3 8. Re2 $11 {is an immediate draw.}) (Kxe7 $144 4. Kg2 b1=Q 5. Rxb1 $11 {is also drawn} (5. Rf7+ Ke6 6. Rxb1 Rxb1 7. Rf4 $11)) 4. Rf8+ Kxe7 5. R8f7+ Ke6 6. R7f6+ Ke5 ({If Black plays his king to the b-file by} Kd5 $144 7. R6f5+ Kc4 (Kd4 $144 8. R5f4+ Kd3 9. Kg2 b1=Q 10. R1f3+ Kd2 11. Rd4+ $11) 8. R5f4+ Kb3 {then} 9. Rf8 $11 {draws}) 7. R6f5+ Ke4 $1 {Black''s king does not have to stay on the e-file in this line, but the result is the same whether he ends up on c3, d3 or e3, and this move sets a trap.} 8. R5f4+ $1 (8. Rb5 $143 Rxf1+ 9. Kg2 Rf2+ $1 $19 {wins for Black} ({but not} b1=Q $143 10. Rxb1 Rxb1 $11 {stalemate} (Rf2+ $144 11. Kg1 Rh2 12. Rd1 Rxh3 $11))) (8. Kg2 $143 {is too soon; after} b1=Q 9. R1f4+ Ke3 10. Rf3+ Kd4 11. R3f4+ Kc3 12. Rf3+ Kb4 $1 13. R3f4+ Rc4 $19 {the checks come to an end}) Kd3 9. Kg2 $1 {Now is the right time for this move. Black has nothing better than to promote.} b1=Q 10. R1f3+ $1 {The same manoeuvre can be played when the black king is on any square on the third rank, except b3 (in that case R1f3+ can be met by ... Rc3!) , but then White draws by Rf8, as in the note to Black''s 6th move.} Kc2 11. Rc4+ Kd2 (Kd1 $144 12. Rxc1+ $11 {draws} (12. Rd4+ Ke2 13. Re4+ Qxe4 $11 {stalemate})) 12. Rd4+ Ke2 ({Certainly not} Ke1 $143 13. Re3#) 13. Re4+ $1 Qxe4 $11 {Stalemate. Now we see why White had to avoid winning the h4-pawn.}'),
('zA5aPG3','b6','1. b6 (1. a5 $143 Kxe4+ 2. Ke1 Nc7 3. b6 Na6 $19) Kxe4+ (Nd6 $144 2. a5 Kxe4+) 2. Ke1 {Il faudra contrôler la case c3 plus tard} (2. Kd2 $143 Nd6 3. a5 Nc4+ 4. Kc2 Nxa5 $19) Nd6 3. a5 Kf5 (Kxd4 $144 4. a6 Bf3 5. g6 $18) (Kd5 $144 4. b7 Nxb7 5. a6 Kc6 6. a7 $18) 4. g6 (4. Kf2 $143 Bf7 $11) (4. a6 $143 Bf3 $11) Kxg6 (Bxg6 $144 5. b7 Nxb7 6. a6 $18) (Ke6 $144 5. b7 (5. Kf2 $143 Kd7 6. g7 Bf7 $19) Nxb7 6. d5+ Kxd5 7. a6 Kc6 8. a7 $18) 5. Kf2 {Contrôle la case c3} Bg4 6. b7 Nxb7 7. a6 Bc8 8. a7 $18 {"A study based on the surprise move 4.g6!! It is hard to believe that a pawn move on the King''s side of the board is needed to promote a pawn on the other side."}'),
('ZqQR4Ow','Ngf4','1. Ngf4 Bc8 2. g8=Q Rxg8 3. Ne7 Rh8 4. Nxc8 Kg5+ 5. Kg1 Rxc8 6. d7 Rg8 7. d8=R $1 (7. d8=Q+ $143 Kh6+ 8. Qxg8 $11) Kh4+ 8. Ng2+ Kh3 9. Rd2 $18'),
('G38XeKA','Be6','1. Be6 Bc5 $1 (Bc1 $144 2. Rc3 Bd2 (Bb2 $144 3. Rc4 Re8 4. c7 $11 Rf6 5. c8=Q+ Rxc8 6. Bxc8 $11) 3. Rc2 Rf2 4. Bxc8 Rh2+ 5. Kxg3 Bf4+ 6. Kxf4 Rxc2 7. Bd7 $11) 2. Rxg3 $1 (2. Bxc8 $143 Bxe3 3. Bxf5 gxf5 4. Kxg3 Kb8 5. Kf3 Bb6 $19 (Bh6 $19)) (2. Bxf5 $143 gxf5 3. Rxg3 Rxc6 4. Rf3 Rf6 $19) Rxc6 $1 (Rc7 $5 $144 3. Bxf5 gxf5 4. Rf3 $1 Rf7 5. c7 $1 Kb7 6. c8=Q+ $1 Kxc8 7. Rc3 $1 Rc7 8. Rf3 $1 Rf7 9. Rc3 $11 {positional draw.}) 3. Rxg6 $1 Rf3+ $1 (Re5 $144 4. Bd5 $1 $11) 4. Kg4 $1 (4. Kg2 $2 $143 Rf2+ $19) Rf1 $1 5. Bd5 Rg1+ 6. Bg2 $3 $1 Rxg2+ 7. Kh5 $1 $11 {draw.} Rgxg6 $11 {stalemate} (Rcxg6 $144 $11 {stalemate})'),
('PlxD4Xe','Kg2','1. Kg2 (1. Nb6 $143 Kc7 2. Nc4 Nf2 3. Nxa5 Ne4 4. c4 (4. f5 $144 Nxc3 5. f6 Kd8 $11) Nc5 $11) (1. Kxh1 $143 Kb7 2. f5 a4 3. e6 dxe6 4. f6 a3 5. f7 a2 6. f8=Q a1=Q+ $11) Kb7 (Ka7 $144 2. Nc7 a4 3. e6 dxe6 4. Nxe6 Kb6 5. f5 (5. Nd4 $143 a3 6. Kxh1 a2 7. Nc2 $11) a3 6. Nd4 Kc5 7. f6 Kd6 8. Kxh1 a2 9. Nc2 $18) 2. f5 (2. Nb6 $143 Kxb6 3. f5 Kc7 4. f6 Kd8 $19) a4 3. Nb6 Kxb6 (a3 $144 4. Nxd7 a2 5. Nc5+ Kc7 6. Nb3 $18) 4. e6 (4. f6 $143 a3 5. e6 a2 6. exd7 Kc7 $11) dxe6 5. f6 a3 6. f7 a2 7. f8=Q a1=Q 8. Qb8+ Kc5 (Ka6 $144 9. Qa8+ $18) 9. Qb4+ Kd5 10. Qd4# {"The prudent intro by wK, eschewing capture of bS on move 1, facilitates promotion with tempo-gaining check for a mid-board mate. The sacrifice of wS at the right moment drops bK onto an unfortunate square. A real conundrum!"}'),
('p8fwWbr','Re7','1. Re7 $1 (1. Rg3 $143 Ba5 2. Bg7 Ne4+ 3. Kxe2 Nxg3+ 4. Kd3 Nh5 5. Ba1 Nf4+ 6. Kc4 Ne2 7. Kb3 Nc1+ 8. Kb2 Bd2 9. c4 $11) (1. Rd3 $143 Ba5 2. Bg7 Nb3+ 3. Kxe2 Nc1+ $11) (1. Rh3+ $143 $1 Kg2 2. Rh6 Ne4 3. Rxb6 Nxc3 $11) (1. Re8 $143 Ba5 2. Bh8 a1=Q+ 3. Bxa1 Nb3+ 4. Kxe2 Nxa1 5. Ra8 Bc3 $11) (1. Re6 $143 Nf3+ 2. Kxe2 Nd4+ $11) Ba5 2. Bh8 $1 a1=Q+ (Ne4+ $144 3. Kxe2 Nc3+ (Bc3 $144 4. Bxc3 Nxc3+ 5. Kf2 Nd1+ 6. Kg3 $1 $18) 4. Kf3 $1 a1=Q 5. Rh7+ Kg1 6. Bd4+ $18) 3. Bxa1 Nb3+ 4. Kxe2 Nxa1 5. Ra7 $1 Bc3 6. Kf1 $1 Kh2 (Be5 $144 7. Ra5 Nxc2 8. Rxe5 Kh2 9. Re2+ Kh1 10. Re4 $18) 7. Ra2 $3 Be5 $1 (Kh1 $144 8. Ra3 $18) (Nxc2 $144 8. Rxc2+ $18) 8. c3+ $1 Kg3 9. Rxa1 Bxc3 10. Ra3 $18'),
('Qt5YjHj','Kd6','1. Kd6 Rd8+ 2. Kc7 Rd7+ 3. Kc6 Ra7 $1 (Rd3 $144 4. Re2+ Kd8 5. Bg5+ Kc8 6. Re8+ Rd8 7. Rxd8#) 4. Rg8+ (4. Be3 $143 Ra6+ $1 5. Bb6 a3 6. Kb5 a2 $11) Ke7 5. Bf8+ $1 Kf6 (Ke6 $144 6. Bc5 Ra6+ 7. Kb5 (7. Bb6 $143 a3 8. Kb5 a2 $11)) 6. Bc5 Ra6+ 7. Bb6 (7. Kb5 $143 Re6 $11) a3 8. Kb5 a2 9. Bd4+ $1 $18'),
('vgng2lI','c8=Q','1. c8=Q Qf1+ $1 (g2+ $144 2. Kh2 Qd6+ 3. Kg1 $18) 2. Rxf1 g2+ 3. Kh2 gxf1=Q (gxf1=N+ $144 4. Kh3 d1=Q 5. Qg4+ $18) 4. Qf5+ $1 (4. Qxb7+ $143 Kxf2 5. Qf7+ Ke2 6. Qc4+ Kf2 7. Qf4+ Ke2 8. Qg4+ Qf3 $11) Ke2 5. Qg4+ Kxf2 (Kd3 $144 6. Qc4#) (Ke1 $144 6. Nc2+ Kxf2 7. Qf4+ Ke2 8. Qe4+ Kd1 9. Ne3+ $18) 6. Nc2 $1 Nd6 (d1=N $144 $1 {main} 7. Qf4+ Ke2 8. Nd4+ Ke1 9. Qe4+ $1 Kd2 10. Nb3#) (d1=Q $144 7. Qg3+ Ke2 8. Qe3#) (Nc5 $143 7. Qf4+ Ke2 8. Qc4+ Nd3 9. Qe4+ Kd1 10. Ne3+ Kc1 11. Qc4+ Kxb2 12. Qc2+ Ka3 13. Nxf1 $18) 7. b3 $1 h5 (d1=N $144 8. Qf4+ Ke2 9. Nd4+ Ke1 10. Nf3+ Ke2 11. Ng1+ Ke1 12. Qb4+ Nc3 13. Qxc3+ Kd1 14. Qa1+ $18) (d1=Q $144 8. Qg3+ Ke2 9. Qe3#) (Nf7 $144 8. Qf4+ Ke2 9. Qe4+ Kd1 10. Ne3+ $18) (Nf5 $144 8. Qxf5+ Ke2 9. Qe4+ Kd1 10. Ne3+ $18) 8. Qf4+ Ke2 9. Qe5+ Kd3 (Kf3 $144 10. Nd4+ Kg4 11. Qg3#) (Ne4 $144 10. Qxe4+ Kd1 11. Ne3+ $18) 10. Nb4#'),
