('c40S3Ok','Nc7','1. Nc7+ $1 (1. h8=Q $143 Qb7+ $19) (1. Kh1 $143 Be5 $19) Qxc7 2. Kh1 $1 Qxh7 (Qb7+ $144 3. Bg2 Be5 4. Be1 Qxg2+ 5. Kxg2 Kb7 6. Bxg3 $18) 3. Bg2+ Qb7 4. c6 Qc7 $1 $18 {Switchback} (Qxb4 $144 5. c7+ Qb7 6. c8=Q $18) 5. a3 $1 ({Thematic try} 5. Ba5 $143 a3 {zz} 6. Bb4 a5 7. Bxa5 a6 8. Bb6 a5 $1 $11) (5. Bc5 $143 a3 $1 6. Bb4 a5 $11) a5 6. Bc5 $1 (6. Bxa5 $143 a6 7. Bb6 a5 $19) a6 7. Bb6 $1 {zz} Qxb6 ({main} Qc8 $144 8. c7+ Qb7 {Switchback} 9. c8=R $1 (9. c8=Q $143 Qxg2+ 10. Kxg2 h1=Q+ 11. Kxh1 g2+ 12. Kg1 $11 {stalemate wit pinned bishop}) (9. c8=B $143 Qxg2+ 10. Kxg2 Bd6 $11) (9. c8=N $143 Qxg2+ 10. Kxg2 Kb7 $19) (9. Bxb7+ $143 Kxb7 10. cxb8=Q+ Kxb8 $11) Qxg2+ 10. Kxg2 h1=Q+ 11. Kxh1 g2+ 12. Kxg2 $18) ({or also} Qxc6 $144 8. Bxc6#) (Ba7 $144 8. Bxc7 $18) 8. c7+ Ka7 9. c8=N# $1 {Phenix. Two different zz (in thematic try and main line), two underpromotions - to knight and rook! ---------- An excellent synthesis of classical and modern ideas!}'),
('ISQ22wN','Rg3','{I thank Oleg Efrosinin for entrusting me with the task of judging the studies section of the 20th Birnov MT. From Oleg I received 36 studies with solutions. I eliminated a few studies for lack of originality. Then a few more were eliminated for lack of polish. And yet a few more were eliminated for an apparent lack of theme. The remaining 13 studies were of satisfactory quality. I tested these 13 for soundness and found mistakes in only three. Here are the 10 awarded studies. .} 1. Rg3+ Kh7 $1 2. Rg7+ $3 ({The thematic try is} 2. Rxg2 $143 Qxd3 3. Bc2 Kxh6 4. Rg6+ Qxg6 5. Bxg6 Kxg6 6. Kg4 d3 $1 7. Kf3 Kg5 8. Ke3 Kh4 9. Kxd3 Kxh3 10. Kc4 Kg4 11. Kb5 Kf5 12. Kc6 Ke6 13. Kb7 Kd7 14. Kxa7 Kc7 {=}) Kxh6 3. Rxg2 Qxd3 4. Bc2 {zz} Qxa6 5. Rg6+ Qxg6 6. Bxg6 Kxg6 7. Kg4 d3 8. Kf3 Kg5 9. Ke3 Kh4 10. Kxd3 Kxh3 11. Kc4 Kg4 12. Kb5 Kf5 13. Ka6 Ke6 14. Kxa7 $18 {The winning study exhibits a cleverly constructed zugzwang position in which, with Black to play, an obstrusive wPa6 is captured. The thematic try is identical to the solution except that the wPa6 remains on board. The importance of the pawn''s capture is revealed only after several moves. A fine example of the modern thematic try (or "look ahead") study.}'),
('5mzFhcz','Nd7','1. Nd7 $1 Kxd7 2. e6+ Ke8 (Kc8 $144 3. exf7 Qe5+ 4. Kh4 Qe4+ 5. g4 Qxe1+ 6. Kh5 Qe5+ 7. g5 Qe2+ 8. Kh6 Qe6+ 9. Kg7 Qg6+ 10. Kf8 $18) 3. Bc3 Ne5 4. Kh6 $1 ({Thematic try} 4. Bd4 $143 Qg7 5. Nc7+ Kxe7 6. Bc5+ Kd8 7. e7+ Kxc7 $1 (Qxe7 $144 8. Bxe7+ Kxe7 9. Kh6 $11) 8. e8=N+ $1 Kc6 9. Nxg7 Kxc5 10. Kh6 a4 11. Kxh7 Nd3 12. g4 Nxb2 13. Ne6+ Kd6 14. g5 a3 15. g6 a2 16. g7 a1=Q 17. g8=Q Qb1+ 18. Kh6 Qf5 19. Ng5 Nd3 20. h4 Nf4 $11) a4 5. Kh5 $1 (5. g4 $143 a3 $1 6. bxa3 Nxg4+ 7. hxg4 Qe5 8. Nf6+ Qxf6+ 9. Bxf6 $11 {pat.}) Qg7 6. Nc7+ Kxe7 7. Bb4+ Kd8 8. e7+ Kxc7 9. e8=N+ $1 $18'),
